v0.098: Backup & Restore (full data + secrets), seeded login renamed to admin

- Added Settings -> Backup & Restore: "Download Full Backup" produces one
  .zip with a full pg_dump (every order, product, stock item, ticket,
  company, and every Settings field - all DB-backed) plus secrets.env, the
  connection secrets that only ever live in .env and never touch the
  database (Postgres credentials, SMTP account, Shopify Client ID/Secret).
  "Restore into THIS system" replaces the current database from an
  uploaded backup (type RESTORE to confirm - cannot be undone); the
  backup's secrets are listed but never auto-applied to a running
  container, since Docker only reads .env at container start.
- Added restore.sh (repo root) - stands a brand new machine up from a
  backup in one command: writes .env from the backup's secrets, imports
  the database, brings up the full stack. Added backup.sh as the
  command-line equivalent of the in-app download, running pg_dump inside
  the postgres container itself (always version-matched, cron-friendly).
- backend/Dockerfile now installs postgres client tools (pg_dump/psql) so
  the in-app Backup & Restore buttons actually work - needs a rebuild
  (docker compose up --build) to pick up.
- Bumped the multipart upload limit 20MB -> 200MB (application.yml) so
  restoring a backup isn't capped by the old stock-import-sized limit.
- Renamed the seeded first-login user from "Dan Cheetham" to "admin" (same
  ChangeMe123! temporary password) - FirstUserSeeder, README.
- Folded the new Backup & Restore instructions into
  docs/BNS_Warehouse_Setup_Guide.pdf as a new Section 10, renumbering the
  former "Known Gaps" to Section 11 and dropping its now-solved
  "no backup strategy" bullet.

